'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-vo-j-006-lut-share-block-load-and-spin2.spin2
''   Purpose.... VO-J-006 arms D and F on SILICON: does a block load (SETQ2 + RDLONG) into the sender's LUT reach the
''               partner cog's LUT, and what happens with a Spin2 cog as the sender (its start-up block loads, and its
''               own WRLUTs), depending on when the receiver executes SETLUTS #1?  Plus: does SETLUTS survive a COGINIT?
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... Oct 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED  (register VO-J-006, arms D and F; close-out study step 8; bench-groupD-recheck.md section 6)

  What the sources say (silicon-doc-text.txt:491-504): adjacent cogs whose IDs differ only in the LSB "can each allow their lookup
  RAMs to be written by the other cog via its local lookup RAM writes"; SETLUTS #0 = "disallow writes from other cog (default)",
  SETLUTS #1 = "allow writes from other cog"; COGINIT with %x_1_xxx1 finds and starts an even/odd pair "with the same parameters".
  GETBRK WC returns "D[26] = 1 if LUT sharing enabled (established by SETLUTS)" (:2565).  Arms A, B, C, E of the filed row are
  answered by that text (recheck section 6) and are run here only as CONTROLS.  What no source states:
    D : which writes count as "local lookup RAM writes"?  WRLUT is the obvious one; the Spin2 interpreter fills its LUT by a
        SETQ2 + RDLONG BLOCK load (Spin2_interpreter.spin2:2044-2048: "setq2 #(lut_code-1) & $1FF / rdlong 0,ptrb" clears LUT
        $000..$00F and "setq2 #lut_end-lut_code-1 / rdlong lut_code & $1FF,rdf" loads the interpreter into LUT $010..).  Does a
        block load into the sender's LUT arrive in the receiver's LUT?
    F : with a Spin2 cog as sender (the interpreter owns LUT $010..$1FF, spin2-v55-text.txt:806, :834; LUT $000..$00F is free for
        any use), does the interpreter's LUT content arrive in a receiver that executed SETLUTS #1 before the launch?  after
        it?  Does a WRLUT executed by Spin2 inline PASM arrive?
    S : is the SETLUTS state kept when a cog is COGINITed again (the silicon-doc says only that locks are released at COGINIT,
        :3698)?  Two small arms: restart the receiver after SETLUTS #1 (S1); restart the sender (S2: does a sender restart disturb the
        RECEIVER's enable -- the sender itself never executed SETLUTS).
  This program MEASURES D, F and S and predicts nothing about them.  Controls with known results gate the rig.

  RIG  (NO PINS, NO JUMPER, NOTHING ATTACHED)
    Cog 0 (Spin2, the only cog with the debugger, DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001) orchestrates and reports.  COGINIT with
    COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR starts an even/odd pair of free cogs; both run the same PASM program `node`, which reads its COGID, announces
    itself, and then executes commands that cog 0 posts to its own command slot in a hub mailbox (one slot per cog: command,
    arg0, arg1).  Cog 0 posts a command and waits for the slot to read 0 (done) -- EVERY ORDERING IS A HANDSHAKE, nothing depends
    on timing.  The even cog is the SENDER, the odd cog the RECEIVER.  Observation = each cog dumps its own 512-long LUT to a hub
    buffer (RDLUT loop) when asked.  The Spin2 sender (arms F) is started with COGSPIN onto the even cog (the same cog id) and
    answers cog 0 through its own mailbox slots with inline PASM (RDLUT dump, WRLUT).  No debug() is ever executed outside cog 0.

  COMMANDS OF `node` (cog 0 -> a pair cog)
    1 SETLUTS a0 (0 / 1)     2 FILL a0     (LUT[i] := a0 + i for i = 0..511, local WRLUTs)
    3 WRLIST a0 (hub address of  count, addr0, val0, addr1, val1 ... : WRLUT val, addr)
    4 BLOCK_A  SETQ2 #127 / RDLONG $040, blk   (128 longs into LUT $040..$0BF)
    5 BLOCK_B  SETQ2 #63  / RDLONG $1C0, blk   (64 longs into LUT $1C0..$1FF, the top of the LUT)
    6 DUMP     (own LUT $000..$1FF -> the cog's dump buffer in hub)       7 GETFLAG (GETBRK WC, D[26] -> hub)

  PATTERNS (all distinct): receiver fill PAT_R + i = $5A5A_0000 + i ; sender fill PAT_S + i = $A5A5_0000 + i ; block source
  BLK + i = $B10C_0000 + i ; WRLIST values V_k = $C0DE_0000 + k at LUT $000, $0FF, $100, $1FF ; Spin2 WRLIST XV_k = $5E1D_0000 + k at
  LUT $000, $005, $00A, $00F.

  ARMS (each starts from a fresh COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR; as soon as the pair has announced, cog 0 sends SETLUTS #0 to BOTH cogs, so every arm
  starts with sharing explicitly disabled whatever state a stopped cog may have retained; ROUNDS rounds.  If the pair does not start,
  the arm returns at once with its handshake flag false -- no later command and no restart is issued with a missing cog id)
    NEG   S FILL(PAT_S) ; R FILL(PAT_R) ; [receiver stays at SETLUTS #0] ; S WRLIST(V) ; dumps
          CONTROL: the receiver is UNCHANGED everywhere (512 of 512 = PAT_R) and the sender holds V (4 of 4).
    POS   S FILL(PAT_S) ; R FILL(PAT_R) ; R SETLUTS(1) ; S WRLIST(V) ; dumps
          CONTROL: V arrives at the receiver (4 of 4) and nothing else changes (508 of 508).
    DIR   S FILL(PAT_S) ; R SETLUTS(1) ; R FILL(PAT_R) ; sender dump
          CONTROL (direction): the sender is UNCHANGED (512 of 512 = PAT_S): the receiver's own writes do not reach a sender
          that never enabled.
    BLK0  S FILL ; R FILL ; [R at SETLUTS #0] ; S BLOCK_A ; S BLOCK_B ; dumps
          CONTROL: the block load lands in the SENDER (128 + 64 of 192) and nothing arrives at the receiver (512 of 512 = PAT_R).
    BLK   S FILL ; R FILL ; R SETLUTS(1) ; S BLOCK_A ; S BLOCK_B ; dumps          <- ARM D
          sender local gate: 128 + 64 of 192.  Measured: how many of the 128 + 64 longs arrived in the receiver, and whether
          anything else changed.
    F1    R FILL(PAT_R) ; R SETLUTS(1) ; COGSPIN the Spin2 sender onto the even cog ; wait for "spin up" ; X DUMP (Spin2
          inline-PASM RDLUT of its own LUT) ; R DUMP (dump 1) ; X WRLIST(XV) (inline-PASM WRLUT) ; R DUMP (dump 2)   <- ARM F, before
    F2    R FILL(PAT_R) ; [receiver at SETLUTS #0] ; COGSPIN the Spin2 sender ; wait ; X DUMP ; R DUMP (dump 1) ; R SETLUTS(1) ;
          X WRLIST(XV) ; R DUMP (dump 2)                                                                      <- ARM F, after
          Measured: dump 1 against the Spin2 sender's dump (equal longs of 512), against PAT_R (changed longs of 512), LUT
          $000..$00F zero (16 of 16 if the interpreter's clear arrived); dump 2: the 4 XV values at $000, $005, $00A, $00F.
    S1    S FILL ; R SETLUTS(1) ; R FILL ; GETFLAG ; COGINIT the receiver again (same program, does NOT execute SETLUTS) ; GETFLAG ;
          S WRLIST(V) ; R DUMP.      Measured: GETBRK D[26] before / after the restart and V arrival (4 of 4 = sharing survived).
    S2    S FILL ; R SETLUTS(1) ; R FILL ; COGINIT the sender again ; S WRLIST(V) ; R DUMP.       Measured: V arrival.

  CONTROLS (gating -- a failure prints RIG FAIL and NO VERDICT for D and F)
    W : the pair started with COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR is an even/odd pair (even id, odd id = even + 1), every round of every arm; SETLUTS #0 is
        then sent to both cogs (no arm inherits a sharing state retained by a stopped cog).
    N : NEG and BLK0 leave the receiver unchanged (the rig can see 'no sharing').  K : POS delivers V (4 of 4) and changes nothing else
        (the documented mechanism works).  C : DIR leaves the sender unchanged.  L : BLK0 / BLK land in the sender (128 + 64).
    H : every handshake completes within CMD_TIMEOUT; the Spin2 sender reports up within SPIN_TIMEOUT.  A timeout is a RIG FAIL.
    G : (S1 only -- it does not gate D, F or S2) GETBRK D[26] reads 0 at the start of S1 (after the explicit SETLUTS #0) and 1 after
        SETLUTS #1; when it does not, the S1 verdict rests on the arrival of writes alone and says so.
    Determinism: ROUNDS = 3 rounds of every arm; a verdict needs all rounds equal.

  PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run; printed by the program; nothing is predicted for D, F, S)
    D  : PROPAGATES (every block long arrived, in every round) | DOES NOT PROPAGATE (none, every round) | PARTIAL (counts printed) |
         INCONCLUSIVE (rounds disagree).
    F1 : IMAGE ARRIVES (the receiver's LUT equals the Spin2 sender's dump at all 512 longs) | NOTHING ARRIVES (the receiver is unchanged,
         512 of 512 = PAT_R) | PARTIAL (counts printed).
    F2 : NOT RETROACTIVE (dump 1 unchanged, 512 of 512 = PAT_R) | START-UP WRITES ARRIVED (changed longs, although the receiver was
         still at SETLUTS #0 during the launch) .
    F  : Spin2 inline WRLUT (dump 2): ARRIVES (4 of 4 XV values) | DOES NOT ARRIVE (0 of 4), in F1 and in F2.
    S1 : SETLUTS SURVIVES A COGINIT OF THE RECEIVER (flag 1 after the restart AND V arrives) | RESET BY COGINIT (flag 0 AND V does not
         arrive) | INCONSISTENT (the flag and the arrival disagree).
    S2 : SENDER RESTART DOES NOT DISTURB THE RECEIVER'S ENABLE (V arrives) | SENDER RESTART DISTURBS THE RECEIVER'S ENABLE (V does not
         arrive).

  CONFIGURATION AND ENCODINGS RELIED ON (no smart-pin words here)
    COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR = %01_0001 (spin2-v55-text.txt:1664; silicon-doc-text.txt:413 / :502).  COGEXEC = %00_0000: coginit(cogid, @node, @mailbox)
    starts a given cog in cogexec mode (restarting it if it runs, :417-:418).  GETBRK WC D[26] (:2565).  LUT block-load D operand =
    the LUT address as a register number (Spin2_interpreter.spin2:2047-2048: "rdlong lut_code & $1FF,rdf").

  DEVIATIONS FROM THE BRIEF (bench-groupD-recheck.md section 6)
    1. The brief gives the arm-F timing as 'SETLUTS #1 before the launch, and again after'; here 'after' (F2) is a separate arm with the
       receiver at SETLUTS #0 during the launch and enabled afterwards, so that the 'before' and 'after' effects cannot be confused.
    2. The 'does sharing survive COGINIT' arm is split in two (S1 restarts the receiver, S2 the sender) and reads the SETLUTS state back
       with GETBRK D[26] as well as by the arrival of writes.
    3. Arm D writes into the sender at two places (LUT $040..$0BF and the top, $1C0..$1FF) so that an address-dependent propagation
       is visible.
    4. The Spin2 sender dumps its own LUT through inline PASM (RDLUT) so that arm F compares the receiver with the sender's actual LUT,
       not with an assumed interpreter image.

  VERIFIED OPCODES AND DATA (pnut-ts -d -l v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the .lst; object offsets, cog addresses in brackets)
    Symbol table (listing): BLKA_LUT = $040, BLKA_N = $80 (128), BLKB_LUT = $1C0, BLKB_N = $40 (64), BLK_LONGS = $80, BLK_BASE = $B10C_0000,
      N_SETLUTS..N_GETFLAG = 1..7, MB_ID_E = 0, MB_ID_O = 1, MB_CMD_E = 2, MB_CMD_O = 5, MB_XCMD = 8, MB_SPINUP = 9, MB_P_SDUMP = $0A,
      MB_P_RDUMP = $0B, MB_P_BLK = $0C, MB_FLAG_E = $0D, MB_FLAG_O = $0E, MB_LONGS = $0F.
    CLKMODE $010009FB, CLKFREQ 200_000_000 (listing).  The node PASM is unchanged by the review fixes (re-compiled: same labels and
      offsets); the fixes are Spin2 (SETLUTS #0 after the pair announces, early returns, the restart_node guard, verdict wording).
    DEBUG: 2 records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.  Hub image: node at object offset $0AC; cog labels: node_poll [$014] node_done [$02A]
      do_setluts [$02C] do_fill [$02E] do_wrlist [$036] do_blka [$03F] do_blkb [$042] do_dump [$045] do_getflag [$04E] lutsz_ [$051];
      registers mb_ [$052] .. blksrc_ [$058] .. q_ [$061].
    Instructions read back from the hub image (the block loads are the point of arm D):
      setq2 #127  $FD64FE29    rdlong $040,blksrc_  $FB008058  (D = $040 = the LUT start address as a register number, S = blksrc_ $058)
      setq2 #63   $FD647E29    rdlong $1C0,blksrc_  $FB038058  (D = $1C0)
      setluts a0_ $FD60B637    getbrk v_ wc  $FD70BC35    wrlong #0,cmdp_  $FC680054    cogid me_  $FD60A601
      The block-load form is the one the Spin2 interpreter uses at Spin2_interpreter.spin2:2047-2048 (D a constant register number).
    The Spin2 inline PASM (x_dump: rdlut lutVal,idx ; x_wrlist: wrlut wrVal,wrAddr) compiled without error in the same listing.

  HOW TO RUN
    1. USB serial connected (DEBUG on P62/P63).  Compile: pnut-ts -d test-vo-j-006-lut-share-block-load-and-spin2.spin2
    2. Load to RAM with DEBUG enabled (pnut-term-ts, or PNut Ctrl-F10).
    3. SAVE THE WHOLE CONSOLE OUTPUT -- it is the only record.
    4. Expected run time: well under a second when every handshake works (27 pair starts, a few hundred commands); the report is about
       80 lines.  Done when you see the "VERDICT VO-J-006 ..." lines, then "=== END ===" and DEBUG_END_SESSION.  A failing handshake costs
       up to 0.2 s (a Spin2 start-up up to 0.5 s) and is printed as RIG FAIL.  No END / DEBUG_END_SESSION line within 60 s = a hang or a
       lost session: power-cycle the board and send the LAST line you saw.
    5. Clock: _clkfreq = 200_000_000 assumes the board's 20 MHz crystal; the listing's CLKMODE is $010009FB (see the VERIFIED block).  All
       waits here are handshakes or clkfreq divisions, not fixed clock counts, so a different crystal changes only the timeouts.
    6. Pins: NONE.  No pin is driven or read, no jumper, nothing needs to be attached (P62/P63 carry DEBUG as usual).  The test uses
       two cogs besides cog 0 (a free even/odd pair; the Spin2 sender of arms F is started onto the even cog of that pair).
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq          = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS        = %0000_0001        ' EF-057: debugger in cog 0 ONLY

  ROUNDS            = 3
  LUT_LONGS         = 512
  CMD_TIMEOUT_DIV   = 5                 ' handshake timeout = clkfreq / 5 = 200 ms
  SPIN_TIMEOUT_DIV  = 2                 ' Spin2 start-up timeout = clkfreq / 2 = 500 ms

  PAT_R             = $5A5A_0000        ' receiver fill: LUT[i] = PAT_R + i
  PAT_S             = $A5A5_0000        ' sender fill
  BLK_BASE          = $B10C_0000        ' block source: BLK_BASE + i
  V_BASE            = $C0DE_0000        ' WRLIST values V_k = V_BASE + k
  XV_BASE           = $5E1D_0000        ' Spin2 WRLIST values

  ' block-load regions (LUT address as a register number, and length)
  BLKA_LUT          = $040
  BLKA_N            = 128
  BLKB_LUT          = $1C0
  BLKB_N            = 64
  BLK_LONGS         = 128               ' the block source buffer

  ' WRLIST addresses
  V_ADDR0           = $000
  V_ADDR1           = $0FF
  V_ADDR2           = $100
  V_ADDR3           = $1FF
  X_ADDR0           = $000
  X_ADDR1           = $005
  X_ADDR2           = $00A
  X_ADDR3           = $00F

CON ' ---- Commands and Mailbox ----
  #0, N_NOP, N_SETLUTS, N_FILL, N_WRLIST, N_BLOCK_A, N_BLOCK_B, N_DUMP, N_GETFLAG
  #0, XC_NONE, XC_DUMP, XC_WRLIST

  ' mailbox longs
  MB_ID_E           = 0                 ' the even cog announces its id here (-1 until it does)
  MB_ID_O           = 1                 ' the odd cog
  MB_CMD_E          = 2                 ' even cog slot: command, arg0, arg1
  MB_CMD_O          = 5                 ' odd cog slot: command, arg0, arg1
  MB_XCMD           = 8                 ' Spin2 sender command
  MB_SPINUP         = 9                 ' the Spin2 sender writes 1 when it is up
  MB_P_SDUMP        = 10                ' hub address of the sender dump buffer (written by cog 0)
  MB_P_RDUMP        = 11                ' hub address of the receiver dump buffer
  MB_P_BLK          = 12                ' hub address of the block source buffer
  MB_FLAG_E         = 13                ' GETFLAG result of the even cog
  MB_FLAG_O         = 14                ' GETFLAG result of the odd cog
  MB_LONGS          = 15
  SLOT_LONGS        = 3

CON ' ---- Arms and Results ----
  #0, A_NEG, A_POS, A_DIR, A_BLK0, A_BLK, A_F1, A_F2, A_S1, A_S2
  ARMS              = 9

  ' per (arm, round) result fields
  #0, RF_RECV_UNCH, RF_RECV_V, RF_SEND_V, RF_SEND_UNCH, RF_BLKA_R, RF_BLKB_R, RF_BLKA_S, RF_BLKB_S, RF_EQ_SEND, RF_CHANGED, RF_ZERO16, RF_X_ARR, RF_UNCH_OUT, RF_FLAG0, RF_FLAG_SET, RF_FLAG1, RF_DIFF, RF_OK
  RF_LONGS          = 18

  ' classes of a quantity over the rounds
  #0, Q_ALL, Q_NONE, Q_PART, Q_VARIES

CON ' ---- Report Parameters ----
  LINE_MAX          = 400
  DEC_TOP           = 1_000_000_000
  DEC_DIGITS        = 10
  DEC_BASE          = 10
  HEX_DIGITS        = 8
  HEX_BITS          = 4
  HEX_GROUP         = 4
  HEX_LETTERS       = 10
  SPIN_STACK_LONGS  = 100

VAR ' ---- Mailbox, Buffers & Analysis State ----
  long mailbox[MB_LONGS]
  long blkSrc[BLK_LONGS]                ' block-load source
  long sdump[LUT_LONGS]                 ' sender LUT dump
  long rdump[LUT_LONGS]                 ' receiver LUT dump (dump 1 / the only dump)
  long listV[9]                         ' count, (addr, val) x 4
  long listX[9]
  long results[ARMS * ROUNDS * RF_LONGS]
  long spinStack[SPIN_STACK_LONGS]
  long evenId, oddId                    ' the pair cogs (-1 = none)
  long curArm, curRound
  long hsFail                           ' handshake failures (loud)
  long fail_count
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos


PUB main() | roundIdx, idx
'' Run the J-006 D+F rig: check constants, run every arm ROUNDS times, report.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local roundIdx - round
' @local idx - loop index

  longfill(@mailbox, 0, MB_LONGS)
  longfill(@results, 0, ARMS * ROUNDS * RF_LONGS)
  repeat idx from 0 to BLK_LONGS - 1
    blkSrc[idx] := BLK_BASE + idx
  listV[0] := 4
  listV[1] := V_ADDR0
  listV[2] := V_BASE + 0
  listV[3] := V_ADDR1
  listV[4] := V_BASE + 1
  listV[5] := V_ADDR2
  listV[6] := V_BASE + 2
  listV[7] := V_ADDR3
  listV[8] := V_BASE + 3
  listX[0] := 4
  listX[1] := X_ADDR0
  listX[2] := XV_BASE + 0
  listX[3] := X_ADDR1
  listX[4] := XV_BASE + 1
  listX[5] := X_ADDR2
  listX[6] := XV_BASE + 2
  listX[7] := X_ADDR3
  listX[8] := XV_BASE + 3
  mailbox[MB_P_SDUMP] := @sdump
  mailbox[MB_P_RDUMP] := @rdump
  mailbox[MB_P_BLK] := @blkSrc
  evenId := -1
  oddId := -1
  hsFail := 0
  fail_count := 0
  linePos := 0
  say(string("=== VO-J-006 arms D + F: LUT write-sharing, block-load path and a Spin2 sender; no pins, nothing attached ==="))
  print_predictions()
  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- CONTROL W (construction): constants ---"))
  check_rig_constants()
  if fail_count == 0
    repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
      curRound := roundIdx
      arm_neg_pos(A_NEG, FALSE)
      arm_neg_pos(A_POS, TRUE)
      arm_dir()
      arm_blk(A_BLK0, FALSE)
      arm_blk(A_BLK, TRUE)
      arm_f(A_F1, TRUE)
      arm_f(A_F2, FALSE)
      arm_s1()
      arm_s2()
    stop_pair()
    report()
  else
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a construction control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); nothing was started"))
  finish()


PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  say(string("=== END ==="))
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_u(numVal) | divisor, digitVal, bStarted
' Append an unsigned decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as unsigned

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local digitVal - the digit at that place
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  divisor := DEC_TOP
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat DEC_DIGITS
    digitVal := numVal +/ divisor
    if digitVal <> 0 or bStarted or divisor == 1
      ln_c("0" + digitVal)
      bStarted := TRUE
    numVal := numVal +// divisor
    divisor /= DEC_BASE

PRI ln_d(numVal)
' Append a signed decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as signed

  if numVal < 0
    ln_c("-")
    ln_u(-numVal)
  else
    ln_u(numVal)

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from HEX_DIGITS - 1 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * HEX_BITS)) & $F
    if nibble < HEX_LETTERS
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - HEX_LETTERS)
    if idx == HEX_GROUP
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' pre-registered outcomes and construction controls
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_predictions()
' Print the outcomes fixed before the run.
'

  say(string("PRE-REGISTERED (fixed before the run; nothing is predicted for D, F, S -- no ingested source states them):"))
  say(string("  every arm starts from a fresh COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR; cog 0 posts a command and waits for the cog's slot to read 0 (a handshake, not timing)"))
  say(string("  controls (gate, else RIG FAIL / NO VERDICT for D and F): NEG receiver unchanged 512/512 ; POS V arrives 4/4 and nothing else changes ; DIR sender unchanged 512/512 ;"))
  say(string("                BLK0 block lands in the sender 192/192 and nothing arrives (512/512 unchanged) ; the pair is even/odd ; handshakes complete"))
  say(string("  (S1 only) GETBRK D[26] reads 0 then 1 around SETLUTS #1 -- if not, S1 is judged on arrival alone"))
  say(string("  D  (arm BLK): PROPAGATES = every one of the 128 + 64 block longs arrived, all rounds | DOES NOT PROPAGATE = none arrived, all rounds | PARTIAL | INCONCLUSIVE (rounds differ)"))
  say(string("  F1 (Spin2 sender, receiver enabled BEFORE the launch): IMAGE ARRIVES = receiver LUT equals the Spin2 sender's dump at all 512 | NOTHING ARRIVES = receiver unchanged | PARTIAL"))
  say(string("  F2 (receiver enabled AFTER the launch): NOT RETROACTIVE = dump 1 unchanged | START-UP WRITES ARRIVED = changed longs ; the Spin2 inline WRLUT (4 values) ARRIVES / DOES NOT ARRIVE, in F1 and in F2"))
  say(string("  S1 (receiver COGINITed after SETLUTS #1): SURVIVES = GETBRK D[26] = 1 after the restart AND V arrives | RESET BY COGINIT = flag 0 AND V does not arrive | INCONSISTENT"))
  say(string("  S2 (sender COGINITed): SENDER RESTART DOES NOT DISTURB THE RECEIVER'S ENABLE = V arrives | DISTURBS IT = V does not arrive"))
  say(string("  every arm: after the pair announces, SETLUTS #0 is sent to both cogs, so sharing starts disabled whatever a stopped cog retained"))

PRI check_rig_constants()
' Control W: the constants are what the arms assume.
'

  ln_s(string("  COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR = "))
  ln_h(COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR)
  ln_s(string(" (expected %01_0001 = $0000_0011) ; BLKA "))
  ln_h(BLKA_LUT)
  ln_s(string(" x "))
  ln_u(BLKA_N)
  ln_s(string(" ; BLKB "))
  ln_h(BLKB_LUT)
  ln_s(string(" x "))
  ln_u(BLKB_N)
  ln_s(string(" ; block source "))
  ln_u(BLK_LONGS)
  say(string(" longs"))
  if COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR <> %01_0001
    say(string("RIG FAIL: COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR is not %01_0001"))
    fail_count++
  if BLKA_LUT + BLKA_N - 1 > $1FF or BLKB_LUT + BLKB_N - 1 <> $1FF or BLKA_N > BLK_LONGS or BLKB_N > BLK_LONGS
    say(string("RIG FAIL: block-load regions do not fit the LUT or the source buffer"))
    fail_count++
  if BLKA_LUT + BLKA_N > BLKB_LUT or V_ADDR0 >= BLKA_LUT or V_ADDR1 < BLKA_LUT + BLKA_N or V_ADDR2 >= BLKB_LUT
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the WRLIST addresses overlap the block regions in a way the arms do not expect"))
    fail_count++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' handshakes and pair management
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI stop_pair()
' Stop both cogs of the pair, if started.
'

  if evenId >= 0
    cogstop(evenId)
  if oddId >= 0
    cogstop(oddId)
  evenId := -1
  oddId := -1

PRI fresh_pair() : bOk | startTick, startedCog
' Stop any pair, start a new even/odd pair running `node` and wait until both cogs have announced.
'
' @returns bOk - TRUE when both announced and form an even/odd pair

' Local Variables:
' @local startTick - CT when the wait began
' @local startedCog - the cog COGINIT reports starting (-1 = none free)

  stop_pair()
  mailbox[MB_ID_E] := -1
  mailbox[MB_ID_O] := -1
  longfill(@mailbox[MB_CMD_E], 0, 2 * SLOT_LONGS)
  mailbox[MB_XCMD] := 0
  mailbox[MB_SPINUP] := 0
  startedCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR, @node, @mailbox)
  if startedCog < 0
    bOk := FALSE
  else
    startTick := getct()
    repeat until (mailbox[MB_ID_E] >= 0 and mailbox[MB_ID_O] >= 0) or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq / CMD_TIMEOUT_DIV
    evenId := mailbox[MB_ID_E]
    oddId := mailbox[MB_ID_O]
    bOk := evenId >= 0 and oddId >= 0 and (evenId & 1) == 0 and oddId == evenId + 1
    if bOk == FALSE
      ' a pair that started but did not announce is stopped here, so it cannot hold
      ' cogs the next arm's COGINIT needs (stop_pair only knows announced ids)
      cogstop(startedCog & !1)
      cogstop(startedCog | 1)
      evenId := -1
      oddId := -1
  if bOk == FALSE
    hsFail++
    say(string("RIG FAIL: COGEXEC_NEW_PAIR did not give an even/odd pair that announced"))
  else
    bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_SETLUTS, 0, 0)         ' every arm starts with sharing disabled in both cogs,
    bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 0, 0)         ' whatever state a stopped cog retained

PRI node_cmd(who, cmdCode, arg0, arg1) : bOk | pSlot, startTick
' Post one command to the even (who = 0) or odd (who = 1) cog and wait for its slot to read 0.
'
' @param who - 0 = even cog (sender), 1 = odd cog (receiver)
' @param cmdCode - N_*
' @param arg0 - first argument
' @param arg1 - second argument
' @returns bOk - TRUE when the cog completed the command in time

' Local Variables:
' @local pSlot - mailbox index of the cog's slot
' @local startTick - CT when the wait began

  pSlot := MB_CMD_E + who * SLOT_LONGS
  mailbox[pSlot + 1] := arg0
  mailbox[pSlot + 2] := arg1
  mailbox[pSlot] := cmdCode
  startTick := getct()
  repeat until mailbox[pSlot] == 0 or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq / CMD_TIMEOUT_DIV
  bOk := mailbox[pSlot] == 0
  if bOk == FALSE
    hsFail++
    mailbox[pSlot] := 0
    say(string("RIG FAIL: a pair cog did not complete a command within the handshake timeout"))

PRI restart_node(who) : bOk | pSlot, startTick, tgtCog, pId
' Restart the even or odd cog with the `node` program (COGINIT onto a running cog) and wait for its announcement.
'
' @param who - 0 = even cog, 1 = odd cog
' @returns bOk - TRUE when the cog announced again

' Local Variables:
' @local pSlot - mailbox index of the cog's slot
' @local startTick - CT when the wait began
' @local tgtCog - the cog restarted
' @local pId - mailbox index of the cog's id slot

  pSlot := MB_CMD_E + who * SLOT_LONGS
  pId := MB_ID_E + who
  if who == 0
    tgtCog := evenId
  else
    tgtCog := oddId
  if tgtCog < 0
    ' no cog id (the pair did not start): coginit(-1, ...) would mean "any free cog or pair" and launch a stray pair
    hsFail++
    say(string("RIG FAIL: restart_node has no target cog (the pair did not start); nothing was restarted"))
    bOk := FALSE
    return
  mailbox[pSlot] := 0
  mailbox[pId] := -1
  coginit(tgtCog, @node, @mailbox)
  startTick := getct()
  repeat until mailbox[pId] == tgtCog or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq / CMD_TIMEOUT_DIV
  bOk := mailbox[pId] == tgtCog
  if bOk == FALSE
    hsFail++
    say(string("RIG FAIL: a restarted pair cog did not announce"))

PRI set_res(armIdx, fieldIdx, valueVal)
' Record one result field of the current round.
'
' @param armIdx - A_*
' @param fieldIdx - RF_*
' @param valueVal - the value

  results[(armIdx * ROUNDS + curRound) * RF_LONGS + fieldIdx] := valueVal

PRI get_res(armIdx, roundIdx, fieldIdx) : valueVal
' One recorded result field.
'
' @param armIdx - A_*
' @param roundIdx - round
' @param fieldIdx - RF_*
' @returns valueVal - the value

  valueVal := results[(armIdx * ROUNDS + roundIdx) * RF_LONGS + fieldIdx]

PRI count_eq(pDump, baseVal, firstIdx, lastIdx) : countVal | idx
' How many longs of a dump equal baseVal + index over an index range.
'
' @param pDump - hub address of a 512-long dump
' @param baseVal - the pattern base
' @param firstIdx - first index
' @param lastIdx - last index
' @returns countVal - matches

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - index

  countVal := 0
  repeat idx from firstIdx to lastIdx
    if long[pDump][idx] == baseVal + idx
      countVal++

PRI count_v(pDump, pList, baseVal) : countVal | idx
' How many of the four WRLIST (address, value) pairs are present in a dump.
'
' @param pDump - hub address of a 512-long dump
' @param pList - hub address of the WRLIST (count, addr, val ...)
' @param baseVal - unused, kept for symmetry
' @returns countVal - pairs whose value is at its address

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - pair index

  countVal := 0
  repeat idx from 0 to long[pList][0] - 1
    if long[pDump][long[pList][1 + idx * 2]] == long[pList][2 + idx * 2]
      countVal++

PRI count_unch(pDump, baseVal, bExcludeV, bExcludeBlk) : countVal | idx, bSkip
' How many longs equal baseVal + index, leaving out the WRLIST addresses and/or the two block regions.
'
' @param pDump - hub address of a 512-long dump
' @param baseVal - the pattern base
' @param bExcludeV - TRUE leaves out the four V addresses
' @param bExcludeBlk - TRUE leaves out the two block-load regions
' @returns countVal - matches in the places that were not left out

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - index
' @local bSkip - this index is left out

  countVal := 0
  repeat idx from 0 to LUT_LONGS - 1
    bSkip := FALSE
    if bExcludeV and (idx == V_ADDR0 or idx == V_ADDR1 or idx == V_ADDR2 or idx == V_ADDR3)
      bSkip := TRUE
    if bExcludeBlk and ((idx >= BLKA_LUT and idx < BLKA_LUT + BLKA_N) or (idx >= BLKB_LUT and idx < BLKB_LUT + BLKB_N))
      bSkip := TRUE
    if bSkip == FALSE and long[pDump][idx] == baseVal + idx
      countVal++

PRI count_blk(pDump, firstIdx, countN) : countVal | idx
' How many longs of a block region equal the block source pattern.
'
' @param pDump - hub address of a 512-long dump
' @param firstIdx - first LUT address of the region
' @param countN - length of the region
' @returns countVal - longs equal to BLK_BASE + (index - firstIdx)

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - index within the region

  countVal := 0
  repeat idx from 0 to countN - 1
    if long[pDump][firstIdx + idx] == BLK_BASE + idx
      countVal++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' the arms (each from a fresh pair)
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI arm_neg_pos(armIdx, bEnable) | bOk
' NEG (receiver at the default SETLUTS #0) and POS (receiver SETLUTS #1): the sender fills, the receiver fills,
' the sender WRLUTs the four V values; both LUTs are dumped.
'
' @param armIdx - A_NEG or A_POS
' @param bEnable - TRUE for POS

' Local Variables:
' @local bOk - every handshake completed

  bOk := fresh_pair()
  if bOk == FALSE
    set_res(armIdx, RF_OK, FALSE)
    return
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_FILL, PAT_S, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_FILL, PAT_R, 0)
  if bEnable
    bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 1, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_WRLIST, @listV, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_DUMP, 0, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_DUMP, 0, 0)
  set_res(armIdx, RF_OK, bOk)
  set_res(armIdx, RF_RECV_UNCH, count_eq(@rdump, PAT_R, 0, LUT_LONGS - 1))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_RECV_V, count_v(@rdump, @listV, 0))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_SEND_V, count_v(@sdump, @listV, 0))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_UNCH_OUT, count_unch(@rdump, PAT_R, TRUE, FALSE))

PRI arm_dir() | bOk
' DIR: the receiver enables and fills its own LUT; the sender (never enabled) must be unchanged.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local bOk - every handshake completed

  bOk := fresh_pair()
  if bOk == FALSE
    set_res(A_DIR, RF_OK, FALSE)
    return
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_FILL, PAT_S, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 1, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_FILL, PAT_R, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_DUMP, 0, 0)
  set_res(A_DIR, RF_OK, bOk)
  set_res(A_DIR, RF_SEND_UNCH, count_eq(@sdump, PAT_S, 0, LUT_LONGS - 1))

PRI arm_blk(armIdx, bEnable) | bOk
' BLK0 / BLK (arm D): the sender block-loads two regions of its own LUT (SETQ2 + RDLONG); both LUTs are dumped.
'
' @param armIdx - A_BLK0 or A_BLK
' @param bEnable - TRUE when the receiver executes SETLUTS #1 first

' Local Variables:
' @local bOk - every handshake completed

  bOk := fresh_pair()
  if bOk == FALSE
    set_res(armIdx, RF_OK, FALSE)
    return
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_FILL, PAT_S, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_FILL, PAT_R, 0)
  if bEnable
    bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 1, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_BLOCK_A, 0, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_BLOCK_B, 0, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_DUMP, 0, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_DUMP, 0, 0)
  set_res(armIdx, RF_OK, bOk)
  set_res(armIdx, RF_BLKA_S, count_blk(@sdump + BLKA_LUT * 4, 0, BLKA_N))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_BLKB_S, count_blk(@sdump + BLKB_LUT * 4, 0, BLKB_N))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_BLKA_R, count_blk(@rdump + BLKA_LUT * 4, 0, BLKA_N))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_BLKB_R, count_blk(@rdump + BLKB_LUT * 4, 0, BLKB_N))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_RECV_UNCH, count_eq(@rdump, PAT_R, 0, LUT_LONGS - 1))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_UNCH_OUT, count_unch(@rdump, PAT_R, FALSE, TRUE))

PRI arm_f(armIdx, bBefore) | bOk, startTick, spinCog, idx, diffFirst, eqCount
' F1 (receiver enabled BEFORE the Spin2 launch) and F2 (AFTER): a Spin2 cog is started onto the even cog;
' it dumps its own LUT and later WRLUTs four values with inline PASM.
'
' @param armIdx - A_F1 or A_F2
' @param bBefore - TRUE for F1

' Local Variables:
' @local bOk - every handshake completed
' @local startTick - CT when the wait for the Spin2 cog began
' @local spinCog - cog id COGSPIN returned
' @local idx - index
' @local diffFirst - first LUT address where the receiver differs from the sender dump (-1 none)
' @local eqCount - longs equal in the receiver dump and the sender dump

  bOk := fresh_pair()
  if bOk == FALSE
    set_res(armIdx, RF_OK, FALSE)
    return
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_FILL, PAT_R, 0)
  if bBefore
    bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 1, 0)
  mailbox[MB_SPINUP] := 0
  mailbox[MB_XCMD] := XC_NONE
  spinCog := cogspin(evenId, spin_sender(), @spinStack)
  if spinCog < 0
    bOk := FALSE
    hsFail++
    say(string("RIG FAIL: COGSPIN of the Spin2 sender failed"))
  startTick := getct()
  repeat until mailbox[MB_SPINUP] == 1 or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq / SPIN_TIMEOUT_DIV
  if mailbox[MB_SPINUP] <> 1
    bOk := FALSE
    hsFail++
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the Spin2 sender did not report up"))
  else
    bOk &= x_cmd(XC_DUMP)                       ' the Spin2 sender's own LUT -> sdump
    bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_DUMP, 0, 0)            ' receiver dump 1 -> rdump
    set_res(armIdx, RF_CHANGED, LUT_LONGS - count_eq(@rdump, PAT_R, 0, LUT_LONGS - 1))
    set_res(armIdx, RF_RECV_UNCH, count_eq(@rdump, PAT_R, 0, LUT_LONGS - 1))
    diffFirst := -1
    eqCount := 0
    repeat idx from 0 to LUT_LONGS - 1
      if rdump[idx] == sdump[idx]
        eqCount++
      elseif diffFirst < 0
        diffFirst := idx
    set_res(armIdx, RF_EQ_SEND, eqCount)
    set_res(armIdx, RF_DIFF, diffFirst)
    set_res(armIdx, RF_ZERO16, 16 - count_nonzero(@rdump, 0, 15))
    if bBefore == FALSE
      bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 1, 0)
    bOk &= x_cmd(XC_WRLIST)                     ' Spin2 inline-PASM WRLUT of the four XV values
    bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_DUMP, 0, 0)            ' receiver dump 2 -> rdump
    set_res(armIdx, RF_X_ARR, count_v(@rdump, @listX, 0))
  set_res(armIdx, RF_OK, bOk)

PRI count_nonzero(pDump, firstIdx, lastIdx) : countVal | idx
' How many longs of a dump range are non-zero.
'
' @param pDump - hub address of a 512-long dump
' @param firstIdx - first index
' @param lastIdx - last index
' @returns countVal - non-zero longs

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - index

  countVal := 0
  repeat idx from firstIdx to lastIdx
    if long[pDump][idx] <> 0
      countVal++

PRI x_cmd(xCode) : bOk | startTick
' Post a command to the Spin2 sender and wait for it to clear.
'
' @param xCode - XC_*
' @returns bOk - TRUE when the Spin2 sender completed the command in time

' Local Variables:
' @local startTick - CT when the wait began

  mailbox[MB_XCMD] := xCode
  startTick := getct()
  repeat until mailbox[MB_XCMD] == XC_NONE or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq / SPIN_TIMEOUT_DIV
  bOk := mailbox[MB_XCMD] == XC_NONE
  if bOk == FALSE
    hsFail++
    mailbox[MB_XCMD] := XC_NONE
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the Spin2 sender did not complete a command within the timeout"))

PRI arm_s1() | bOk
' S1: the receiver enables, fills, is restarted with COGINIT (the program does not execute SETLUTS again);
' the flag is read before and after with GETBRK; the sender then WRLUTs V.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local bOk - every handshake completed

  bOk := fresh_pair()
  if bOk == FALSE
    set_res(A_S1, RF_OK, FALSE)
    return
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_GETFLAG, 0, 0)
  set_res(A_S1, RF_FLAG0, (mailbox[MB_FLAG_O] >> 26) & 1)            ' RF_FLAG0: the flag at the start (expected 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_FILL, PAT_S, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 1, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_GETFLAG, 0, 0)
  set_res(A_S1, RF_FLAG_SET, (mailbox[MB_FLAG_O] >> 26) & 1)          ' RF_FLAG_SET: the flag after SETLUTS #1 (expected 1)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_FILL, PAT_R, 0)
  bOk &= restart_node(1)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_GETFLAG, 0, 0)
  set_res(A_S1, RF_FLAG1, (mailbox[MB_FLAG_O] >> 26) & 1)            ' RF_FLAG1: the flag after the COGINIT
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_WRLIST, @listV, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_DUMP, 0, 0)
  set_res(A_S1, RF_OK, bOk)
  set_res(A_S1, RF_RECV_V, count_v(@rdump, @listV, 0))
  set_res(A_S1, RF_UNCH_OUT, count_unch(@rdump, PAT_R, TRUE, FALSE))

PRI arm_s2() | bOk
' S2: the sender is restarted with COGINIT after the receiver enabled; the sender then WRLUTs V.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local bOk - every handshake completed

  bOk := fresh_pair()
  if bOk == FALSE
    set_res(A_S2, RF_OK, FALSE)
    return
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_FILL, PAT_S, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_SETLUTS, 1, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_FILL, PAT_R, 0)
  bOk &= restart_node(0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(0, N_WRLIST, @listV, 0)
  bOk &= node_cmd(1, N_DUMP, 0, 0)
  set_res(A_S2, RF_OK, bOk)
  set_res(A_S2, RF_RECV_V, count_v(@rdump, @listV, 0))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' the Spin2 sender (arms F): runs in the even cog after COGSPIN; every LUT access is inline PASM
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI spin_sender() | xCode
' Report up, then serve cog 0's commands forever.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local xCode - the command read

  mailbox[MB_SPINUP] := 1
  repeat
    xCode := mailbox[MB_XCMD]
    case xCode
      XC_DUMP:
        x_dump()
        mailbox[MB_XCMD] := XC_NONE
      XC_WRLIST:
        x_wrlist()
        mailbox[MB_XCMD] := XC_NONE

PRI x_dump() | idx, lutVal
' Copy this cog's LUT $000..$1FF into sdump with inline-PASM RDLUT.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - LUT address
' @local lutVal - the long read

  repeat idx from 0 to LUT_LONGS - 1
    org
        rdlut   lutVal, idx
    end
    sdump[idx] := lutVal

PRI x_wrlist() | idx, wrAddr, wrVal
' WRLUT the (address, value) pairs of listX with inline PASM.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - pair index
' @local wrAddr - LUT address
' @local wrVal - value

  repeat idx from 0 to listX[0] - 1
    wrAddr := listX[1 + idx * 2]
    wrVal := listX[2 + idx * 2]
    org
        wrlut   wrVal, wrAddr
    end

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' report
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI all_rounds(armIdx, fieldIdx, expVal) : bAll | roundIdx
' Whether a field equals a value in every round.
'
' @param armIdx - A_*
' @param fieldIdx - RF_*
' @param expVal - the value
' @returns bAll - TRUE when every round matches

' Local Variables:
' @local roundIdx - round

  bAll := TRUE
  repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
    if get_res(armIdx, roundIdx, fieldIdx) <> expVal
      bAll := FALSE

PRI class_of(armIdx, fieldIdx, fullVal) : classVal | roundIdx, firstVal, bSame
' Class of a count over the rounds: all of fullVal, none, partial, or the rounds differ.
'
' @param armIdx - A_*
' @param fieldIdx - RF_*
' @param fullVal - the count meaning 'all'
' @returns classVal - Q_ALL, Q_NONE, Q_PART or Q_VARIES

' Local Variables:
' @local roundIdx - round
' @local firstVal - round 0's value
' @local bSame - every round equals round 0

  firstVal := get_res(armIdx, 0, fieldIdx)
  bSame := TRUE
  repeat roundIdx from 1 to ROUNDS - 1
    if get_res(armIdx, roundIdx, fieldIdx) <> firstVal
      bSame := FALSE
  if bSame == FALSE
    classVal := Q_VARIES
  elseif firstVal == fullVal
    classVal := Q_ALL
  elseif firstVal == 0
    classVal := Q_NONE
  else
    classVal := Q_PART

PRI print_arm(armIdx, pName, field1, field2, field3, field4)
' Print one arm's per-round values for up to four result fields.
'
' @param armIdx - A_*
' @param pName - arm name
' @param field1 - RF_* or -1
' @param field2 - RF_* or -1
' @param field3 - RF_* or -1
' @param field4 - RF_* or -1

  print_field(armIdx, pName, field1)
  print_field(armIdx, pName, field2)
  print_field(armIdx, pName, field3)
  print_field(armIdx, pName, field4)

PRI print_field(armIdx, pName, fieldIdx) | roundIdx
' Print one result field over the rounds.
'
' @param armIdx - A_*
' @param pName - arm name
' @param fieldIdx - RF_* or -1 (nothing printed)

' Local Variables:
' @local roundIdx - round

  if fieldIdx >= 0
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_s(pName)
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_s(field_name(fieldIdx))
    ln_c(":")
    repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
      ln_c(" ")
      ln_d(get_res(armIdx, roundIdx, fieldIdx))
    ln_out()

PRI field_name(fieldIdx) : pText
' Printable name of a result field.
'
' @param fieldIdx - RF_*
' @returns pText - address of the name

  pText := lookupz(fieldIdx: string("receiver unchanged (of 512)"), string("V arrived at receiver (of 4)"), string("V present at sender (of 4)"), string("sender unchanged (of 512)"), string("block A at receiver (of 128)"), string("block B at receiver (of 64)"), string("block A at sender (of 128)"), string("block B at sender (of 64)"), string("receiver equals sender dump (of 512)"), string("receiver changed (of 512)"), string("LUT $000..$00F zero at receiver (of 16)"), string("XV arrived at receiver after the Spin2 WRLUT (of 4)"), string("unchanged outside the written places"), string("GETBRK D[26] at start"), string("GETBRK D[26] after SETLUTS #1"), string("GETBRK D[26] after the COGINIT"), string("first LUT address where receiver and sender dump differ (-1 none)"), string("handshakes ok (-1 = yes)"))

PRI yes_no(bFlag) : pText
' Printable YES / NO.
'
' @param bFlag - TRUE or FALSE
' @returns pText - address of "YES" or "NO"

  if bFlag
    pText := string("YES")
  else
    pText := string("NO")

PRI report() | armIdx, bControls, bFlagOk, qA, qB
' Print the controls and every arm, gate, decide. Single exit.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm
' @local bControls - every control holds
' @local bFlagOk - the GETBRK readback follows SETLUTS (S1 only)
' @local qA - class of block A arrival
' @local qB - class of block B arrival

  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- RAW RESULTS per round ---"))
  print_arm(A_NEG, string("NEG "), RF_RECV_UNCH, RF_SEND_V, RF_RECV_V, RF_OK)
  print_arm(A_POS, string("POS "), RF_RECV_V, RF_SEND_V, RF_UNCH_OUT, RF_OK)
  print_arm(A_DIR, string("DIR "), RF_SEND_UNCH, RF_OK, -1, -1)
  print_arm(A_BLK0, string("BLK0"), RF_BLKA_S, RF_BLKB_S, RF_BLKA_R, RF_BLKB_R)
  print_arm(A_BLK0, string("BLK0"), RF_RECV_UNCH, RF_OK, -1, -1)
  print_arm(A_BLK, string("BLK "), RF_BLKA_S, RF_BLKB_S, RF_BLKA_R, RF_BLKB_R)
  print_arm(A_BLK, string("BLK "), RF_RECV_UNCH, RF_UNCH_OUT, RF_OK, -1)
  print_arm(A_F1, string("F1  "), RF_CHANGED, RF_EQ_SEND, RF_ZERO16, RF_DIFF)
  print_arm(A_F1, string("F1  "), RF_RECV_UNCH, RF_X_ARR, RF_OK, -1)
  print_arm(A_F2, string("F2  "), RF_CHANGED, RF_EQ_SEND, RF_ZERO16, RF_DIFF)
  print_arm(A_F2, string("F2  "), RF_RECV_UNCH, RF_X_ARR, RF_OK, -1)
  print_arm(A_S1, string("S1  "), RF_FLAG0, RF_FLAG_SET, RF_FLAG1, RF_RECV_V)
  print_arm(A_S1, string("S1  "), RF_UNCH_OUT, RF_OK, -1, -1)
  print_arm(A_S2, string("S2  "), RF_RECV_V, RF_OK, -1, -1)
  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- CONTROLS (gate) ---"))
  bControls := TRUE
  if hsFail <> 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_u(hsFail)
    say(string(" handshake / start-up failure(s) were reported above"))
    bControls := FALSE
  repeat armIdx from 0 to ARMS - 1
    if all_rounds(armIdx, RF_OK, TRUE) == FALSE
      bControls := FALSE
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: a handshake of arm index "))
      ln_u(armIdx)
      say(string(" did not complete in every round"))
  bControls &= control(string("W/H: every arm completed its handshakes in every round"), bControls)
  bControls &= control(string("NEG: receiver unchanged 512 of 512, sender holds V 4 of 4"), all_rounds(A_NEG, RF_RECV_UNCH, LUT_LONGS) and all_rounds(A_NEG, RF_SEND_V, 4))
  bControls &= control(string("POS: V arrives 4 of 4, nothing else changes 508 of 508, sender holds V"), all_rounds(A_POS, RF_RECV_V, 4) and all_rounds(A_POS, RF_UNCH_OUT, LUT_LONGS - 4) and all_rounds(A_POS, RF_SEND_V, 4))
  bControls &= control(string("DIR: sender unchanged 512 of 512"), all_rounds(A_DIR, RF_SEND_UNCH, LUT_LONGS))
  bControls &= control(string("BLK0: block lands in the sender (128 + 64) and nothing arrives (512 of 512 unchanged)"), all_rounds(A_BLK0, RF_BLKA_S, BLKA_N) and all_rounds(A_BLK0, RF_BLKB_S, BLKB_N) and all_rounds(A_BLK0, RF_RECV_UNCH, LUT_LONGS))
  bControls &= control(string("BLK: block lands in the sender (128 + 64)"), all_rounds(A_BLK, RF_BLKA_S, BLKA_N) and all_rounds(A_BLK, RF_BLKB_S, BLKB_N))
  bFlagOk := all_rounds(A_S1, RF_FLAG0, 0) and all_rounds(A_S1, RF_FLAG_SET, 1)
  ln_s(string("  G (S1 only): GETBRK D[26] reads 0 at the start and 1 after SETLUTS #1: "))
  ln_s(yes_no(bFlagOk))
  ln_out()
  if bFlagOk == FALSE
    say(string("  (the GETBRK readback does not follow SETLUTS here: the S1 verdict rests on the arrival of writes alone; D, F and S2 are not affected)"))
  say(string(" "))
  if bControls == FALSE
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a gating control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); the results are printed for diagnosis only"))
  else
    say(string("--- VERDICTS ---"))
    qA := class_of(A_BLK, RF_BLKA_R, BLKA_N)
    qB := class_of(A_BLK, RF_BLKB_R, BLKB_N)
    if qA == Q_ALL and qB == Q_ALL
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 D: PROPAGATES - a SETQ2 + RDLONG block load into the sender's LUT arrives in the receiver (128 of 128 and 64 of 64, every round)"))
    elseif qA == Q_NONE and qB == Q_NONE
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 D: DOES NOT PROPAGATE - none of the 128 + 64 block-loaded longs arrived in the receiver (every round); the block landed locally (control L)"))
    elseif qA == Q_VARIES or qB == Q_VARIES
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 D: INCONCLUSIVE - the rounds differ (results above)"))
    else
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 D: PARTIAL - some but not all block-loaded longs arrived (counts above)"))
    verdict_f(A_F1, string("F1 (receiver enabled BEFORE the Spin2 launch)"))
    verdict_f(A_F2, string("F2 (receiver enabled AFTER the Spin2 launch)"))
    verdict_s1(bFlagOk)
    if all_rounds(A_S2, RF_RECV_V, 4)
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S2: SENDER RESTART DOES NOT DISTURB THE RECEIVER'S ENABLE - V arrived (4 of 4, every round) after the sender was COGINITed"))
    elseif all_rounds(A_S2, RF_RECV_V, 0)
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S2: SENDER RESTART DISTURBS THE RECEIVER'S ENABLE - V did not arrive after the sender was COGINITed (every round)"))
    else
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S2: INCONCLUSIVE - the rounds differ (results above)"))

PRI control(pText, bHolds) : bOut
' Print one control and its result; count a failure.
'
' @param pText - the control, as text
' @param bHolds - TRUE when it holds
' @returns bOut - bHolds

  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_s(pText)
  if bHolds
    say(string("  -> ok"))
  else
    say(string("  -> FAILED"))
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: control failed: "))
    say(pText)
    fail_count++
  bOut := bHolds

PRI verdict_f(armIdx, pName) | qEq, qCh, qX
' The verdict lines of one F arm.
'
' @param armIdx - A_F1 or A_F2
' @param pName - arm name, as text

' Local Variables:
' @local qEq - class of 'receiver equals the sender dump'
' @local qCh - class of 'receiver changed'
' @local qX - class of the Spin2 inline WRLUT arrival

  qEq := class_of(armIdx, RF_EQ_SEND, LUT_LONGS)
  qCh := class_of(armIdx, RF_CHANGED, LUT_LONGS)
  qX := class_of(armIdx, RF_X_ARR, 4)
  ln_s(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 "))
  ln_s(pName)
  ln_s(string(": start-up writes: "))
  if qEq == Q_ALL
    if armIdx == A_F2
      ln_s(string("START-UP WRITES ARRIVED - although the receiver was still at SETLUTS #0 during the launch, its LUT equals the Spin2 sender's dump at all 512 longs (every round)"))
    else
      ln_s(string("IMAGE ARRIVES - the receiver's LUT equals the Spin2 sender's dump at all 512 longs (every round)"))
  elseif qCh == Q_VARIES or qEq == Q_VARIES
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - the rounds differ"))
  elseif all_rounds(armIdx, RF_CHANGED, 0)
    if armIdx == A_F2
      ln_s(string("NOT RETROACTIVE - dump 1 is unchanged (512 of 512 = its fill), every round: the start-up writes did not reach a receiver enabled only afterwards"))
    else
      ln_s(string("NOTHING ARRIVES - the receiver is unchanged (512 of 512 = its fill), every round"))
  else
    ln_s(string("PARTIAL - receiver changed at "))
    ln_u(get_res(armIdx, 0, RF_CHANGED))
    ln_s(string(" longs, equals the sender at "))
    ln_u(get_res(armIdx, 0, RF_EQ_SEND))
    ln_s(string(" of 512; LUT $000..$00F zero at "))
    ln_u(get_res(armIdx, 0, RF_ZERO16))
    ln_s(string(" of 16; first difference at LUT "))
    ln_d(get_res(armIdx, 0, RF_DIFF))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 "))
  ln_s(pName)
  ln_s(string(": Spin2 inline WRLUT after the enable: "))
  if qX == Q_ALL
    ln_s(string("ARRIVES (4 of 4, every round)"))
  elseif qX == Q_NONE
    ln_s(string("DOES NOT ARRIVE (0 of 4, every round)"))
  elseif qX == Q_VARIES
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - the rounds differ"))
  else
    ln_s(string("PARTIAL (counts above)"))
  ln_out()

PRI verdict_s1(bFlagOk)
' The verdict line of S1.
'
' @param bFlagOk - TRUE when the GETBRK readback followed SETLUTS in this run (so it may enter the verdict)

  if bFlagOk
    if all_rounds(A_S1, RF_FLAG1, 1) and all_rounds(A_S1, RF_RECV_V, 4)
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S1: SETLUTS SURVIVES A COGINIT OF THE RECEIVER - GETBRK D[26] = 1 after the restart and V arrived (every round)"))
    elseif all_rounds(A_S1, RF_FLAG1, 0) and all_rounds(A_S1, RF_RECV_V, 0)
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S1: SETLUTS IS RESET BY COGINIT - GETBRK D[26] = 0 after the restart and V did not arrive (every round)"))
    else
      say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S1: INCONSISTENT or INCONCLUSIVE - the flag and the arrival disagree, or the rounds differ (results above)"))
  elseif all_rounds(A_S1, RF_RECV_V, 4)
    say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S1: SETLUTS SURVIVES A COGINIT OF THE RECEIVER - V arrived (every round); the GETBRK readback was not usable"))
  elseif all_rounds(A_S1, RF_RECV_V, 0)
    say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S1: SETLUTS IS RESET BY COGINIT - V did not arrive (every round); the GETBRK readback was not usable"))
  else
    say(string("VERDICT VO-J-006 S1: INCONCLUSIVE - the rounds differ (results above)"))

DAT ' ---- Node: the program both pair cogs run ----
' cog 0 posts a command into the cog's slot (command, arg0, arg1); the cog executes it and writes 0 to the command long.
' PTRA = @mailbox on entry.  No debug() here.
DAT             org     0
node            mov     mb_, ptra
                cogid   me_
                mov     cmdp_, mb_
                mov     idp_, mb_
                mov     flgp_, mb_
                mov     tmp_, mb_
                testb   me_, #0                 wc      ' C = 1 for the odd cog (the receiver)
        if_nc   add     cmdp_, #MB_CMD_E * 4
        if_c    add     cmdp_, #MB_CMD_O * 4
        if_nc   add     idp_, #MB_ID_E * 4
        if_c    add     idp_, #MB_ID_O * 4
        if_nc   add     flgp_, #MB_FLAG_E * 4
        if_c    add     flgp_, #MB_FLAG_O * 4
        if_nc   add     tmp_, #MB_P_SDUMP * 4
        if_c    add     tmp_, #MB_P_RDUMP * 4
                rdlong  dmp_, tmp_                      ' this cog's dump buffer
                mov     tmp_, mb_
                add     tmp_, #MB_P_BLK * 4
                rdlong  blksrc_, tmp_                   ' the block source buffer
                wrlong  me_, idp_                       ' announce

node_poll       rdlong  cmd_, cmdp_
                cmp     cmd_, #0                wz
        if_z    jmp     #node_poll
                mov     tmp_, cmdp_
                add     tmp_, #4
                rdlong  a0_, tmp_
                add     tmp_, #4
                rdlong  a1_, tmp_
                cmp     cmd_, #N_SETLUTS        wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_setluts
                cmp     cmd_, #N_FILL           wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_fill
                cmp     cmd_, #N_WRLIST         wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_wrlist
                cmp     cmd_, #N_BLOCK_A        wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_blka
                cmp     cmd_, #N_BLOCK_B        wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_blkb
                cmp     cmd_, #N_DUMP           wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_dump
                cmp     cmd_, #N_GETFLAG        wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_getflag
node_done       wrlong  #0, cmdp_                       ' done -- the last write of every command
                jmp     #node_poll

do_setluts      setluts a0_
                jmp     #node_done

' LUT[i] := a0 + i, i = 0..511: local WRLUTs
do_fill         mov     i_, #0
.l              mov     v_, a0_
                add     v_, i_
                wrlut   v_, i_
                add     i_, #1
                cmp     i_, lutsz_              wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.l
                jmp     #node_done

' a0 = hub address of: count, addr0, val0, addr1, val1 ... ; WRLUT val, addr
do_wrlist       rdlong  n_, a0_
                add     a0_, #4
.l              rdlong  ad_, a0_
                add     a0_, #4
                rdlong  v_, a0_
                add     a0_, #4
                wrlut   v_, ad_
                djnz    n_, #.l
                jmp     #node_done

' block loads into this cog's LUT: SETQ2 n-1 / RDLONG <LUT address as a register number>, hub source
do_blka         setq2   #BLKA_N - 1
                rdlong  BLKA_LUT, blksrc_
                jmp     #node_done

do_blkb         setq2   #BLKB_N - 1
                rdlong  BLKB_LUT, blksrc_
                jmp     #node_done

' own LUT $000..$1FF -> this cog's dump buffer in hub
do_dump         mov     i_, #0
                mov     q_, dmp_
.l              rdlut   v_, i_
                wrlong  v_, q_
                add     q_, #4
                add     i_, #1
                cmp     i_, lutsz_              wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.l
                jmp     #node_done

' GETBRK WC: D[26] = LUT sharing enabled -> the cog's flag long in the mailbox
do_getflag      getbrk  v_                      wc
                wrlong  v_, flgp_
                jmp     #node_done

lutsz_          long    LUT_LONGS

mb_             res     1
me_             res     1
cmdp_           res     1
idp_            res     1
flgp_           res     1
dmp_            res     1
blksrc_         res     1
tmp_            res     1
cmd_            res     1
a0_             res     1
a1_             res     1
i_              res     1
v_              res     1
n_              res     1
ad_             res     1
q_              res     1

